From: TB-X606V kernel project
Subject: [PATCH] cgroup: accept the cpuset_v2_mode v1 mount option (as clone_children)

Android 17 libprocessgroup mounts the v1 cpuset controller with ",noprefix,cpuset_v2_mode". 4.9 does not know the
latter, parse_cgroupfs_options() returns -ENOENT and SetupCgroups fails. clone_children makes new cpusets inherit
cpus/mems from the parent, which is the part of v2 mode Android depends on.

---
diff --git a/kernel/cgroup.c b/kernel/cgroup.c
--- a/kernel/cgroup.c
+++ b/kernel/cgroup.c
@@ -1731,7 +1731,8 @@
 			opts->flags |= CGRP_ROOT_NOPREFIX;
 			continue;
 		}
-		if (!strcmp(token, "clone_children")) {
+		/* Android 17 mounts cpuset with "noprefix,cpuset_v2_mode"; clone_children gives the closest 4.9 behaviour */
+		if (!strcmp(token, "clone_children") || !strcmp(token, "cpuset_v2_mode")) {
 			opts->cpuset_clone_children = true;
 			continue;
 		}
